# snapper: its one window reads an image name typed into it, shows that image in a window of its own, and exits on a click in its own window.
# Pointer into the window first (keys go to the window under the pointer). The name typed is no file, so the program writes its refusal
# line in its window and waits for an event; a click there is a button press and the program exits by itself.
move 40 10
wait
type nosuch.gif
key Return
wait
click 1 40 10
